<title>BELGIUM: Belgian liquidity falls at weekly money tender.</title>
<headline>Belgian liquidity falls at weekly money tender.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said on Monday that liquidity fell at its fixed-rate tender for seven-day advances. Details -</p>
<p>    Value date 18/09	   expiry on 25/09</p>
<p>    Amount allotted	    9.525 bln bfr    (14.575 bln *)</p>
<p>    Interest rate		3.00 pct	    (3.00 pct **)</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids     9.525 bln bfr</p>
<p>Percentage of bids accepted  100</p>
<p>* amount draining from the money market on September 18.</p>
<p>** interest rate at previous tender on September 9.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
